 "title": "South Africa Minimum Wage 2026 and Pension Age Compared",
 "content": "<style>.bd-calc{--c-ink:var(--bd-ink,#15171d);--c-muted:var(--bd-muted,#5d6271);--c-line:var(--bd-line,#e8e2d6);--c-surface:var(--bd-surface-2,#fbf9f5);--c-accent:var(--bd-accent,#e2462c);\n  border:1px solid var(--c-line);border-radius:18px;background:var(--c-surface);padding:22px;margin:1.5em 0 2em;color:var(--c-ink);font-family:var(--bd-sans,system-ui,sans-serif)}\n.bd-calc .bc-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(200px,1fr));gap:14px 18px}\n.bd-calc label{display:block;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;color:var(--c-muted);margin-bottom:6px}\n.bd-calc input,.bd-calc select{width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;font:600 17px/1.3 inherit;padding:10px 12px;border:1px solid var(--c-line);border-radius:10px;background:transparent;color:var(--c-ink)}\n.bd-calc input:focus,.bd-calc select:focus{outline:2px solid var(--c-accent);outline-offset:1px}\n.bd-calc .bc-check{display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center;font-size:15px;color:var(--c-ink)}\n.bd-calc .bc-check input{width:auto}\n.bd-calc .bc-out{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(170px,1fr));gap:12px;margin-top:20px}\n.bd-calc .bc-stat{border:1px solid var(--c-line);border-radius:14px;padding:14px}\n.bd-calc .bc-stat span{display:block;font-size:13px;color:var(--c-muted)}\n.bd-calc .bc-stat b{display:block;font-size:22px;margin-top:4px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;word-break:break-word}\n.bd-calc .bc-stat.bc-main b{color:var(--c-accent)}\n.bd-calc .bc-bar{display:flex;height:14px;border-radius:7px;overflow:hidden;margin:18px 0 6px;background:var(--c-line)}\n.bd-calc .bc-bar i{display:block;height:100%}\n.bd-calc .bc-legend{font-size:13px;color:var(--c-muted);display:flex;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap}\n.bd-calc .bc-legend i{display:inline-block;width:10px;height:10px;border-radius:2px;margin-right:6px}\n.bd-calc .bc-note{font-size:14px;color:var(--c-muted);margin:14px 0 0}\n.bd-calc details{margin-top:16px}\n.bd-calc summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600}\n.bd-calc .bc-table{overflow-x:auto;margin-top:10px}\n.bd-calc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}\n.bd-calc th,.bd-calc td{padding:7px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--c-line);text-align:right;white-space:nowrap}\n.bd-calc th:first-child,.bd-calc td:first-child{text-align:left}\n.bd-calc .bc-title{font:800 21px/1.3 var(--bd-serif,Georgia,serif);margin:0 0 4px;color:var(--c-ink)}\n.bd-calc .bc-sub{font-size:14px;color:var(--c-muted);margin:0 0 16px}\n.bd-calc button{font:600 15px/1 inherit;padding:10px 14px;border-radius:10px;border:1px solid var(--c-line);background:transparent;color:var(--c-ink);cursor:pointer}\n.bd-calc button.bc-primary{background:var(--c-accent);border-color:var(--c-accent);color:#fff}\n.bd-calc .bc-row{display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;margin-top:10px}\n.bd-calc .bc-chips{display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:12px}\n.bd-calc .bc-chip{border:1px solid var(--c-line);border-radius:999px;padding:8px 14px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;font-weight:600}\n.bd-calc .bc-chip.bc-best{border-color:var(--c-accent);color:var(--c-accent)}\n.bd-cta{border:1px solid var(--bd-line,#e8e2d6);border-left:4px solid var(--bd-accent,#e2462c);border-radius:12px;padding:14px 18px;margin:1.2em 0 1.8em;background:var(--bd-surface-2,#fbf9f5)}\n.bd-cta p{margin:0!important}\n</style><script>window.bdCalc=window.bdCalc||{\n  num:function(el){var v=parseFloat(String(el.value).replace(/,/g,''));return isFinite(v)?v:0},\n  money:function(n,cur){\n    if(!isFinite(n))return '\\u2014';\n    var loc=cur==='\\u20B9'?'en-IN':'en-US';\n    return cur+Math.round(n).toLocaleString(loc);\n  },\n  words:function(n,cur){\n    if(cur!=='\\u20B9'||!isFinite(n))return '';\n    if(Math.abs(n)>=1e7)return (n/1e7).toFixed(2)+' crore';\n    if(Math.abs(n)>=1e5)return (n/1e5).toFixed(2)+' lakh';\n    return '';\n  },\n  years:function(months){\n    if(!isFinite(months))return 'Never';\n    var y=Math.floor(months/12),m=Math.round(months%12);\n    if(m===12){y++;m=0}\n    return (y?y+(y===1?' year':' years'):'')+(y&&m?', ':'')+(m?m+(m===1?' month':' months'):'')||'0 months';\n  },\n  bind:function(root,run){\n    var go=function(){try{run()}catch(e){}};\n    root.querySelectorAll('input,select').forEach(function(el){el.addEventListener('input',go);el.addEventListener('change',go)});\n    go();\n  }\n};\n</script>\n<div class=\"seo-post\">\n<p><em>Updated 25 October 2026</em></p>\n<img src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/venkateshramu07-design/My_Repo@f454e428cfeba8f707641b3c3ce3ad0e603c3b37/seo/covers/south-africa-money-facts-2026-800.webp\" srcset=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/venkateshramu07-design/My_Repo@f454e428cfeba8f707641b3c3ce3ad0e603c3b37/seo/covers/south-africa-money-facts-2026-800.webp 800w, https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/venkateshramu07-design/My_Repo@f454e428cfeba8f707641b3c3ce3ad0e603c3b37/seo/covers/south-africa-money-facts-2026-1200.webp 1200w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 780px) 92vw, 680px\" alt=\"South Africa Minimum Wage 2026 and Pension Age Compared\" width=\"1200\" height=\"630\" fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:16px\"/>\n\n<p><strong>Quick answer:</strong> In South Africa in 2026, the minimum wage is R30.23/hour (about $316 a month full time); the state pension age is 60 (Older Persons Grant). The table below puts 6 everyday money measures for South Africa side by side and ranks each one against the other countries in our data, using official figures from national statistics offices, central banks, the OECD and Eurostat.</p>\n\n<p>Most comparisons of South Africa look at one number at a time. This page gathers the figures that matter for working, buying a home, paying bills and retiring in South Africa, so you can see them together and see how South Africa compares. Each section links to our full guide for that topic, which covers every country and lists the original sources, and each dataset can be downloaded free.</p>\n\n<h2>South Africa at a Glance</h2>\n<table class=\"bd-cf\"><thead><tr><th>Measure</th><th>South Africa</th><th>Rank</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>Minimum wage</td><td>R30.23/hour (≈ $316/month)</td><td>4th lowest of 38</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Pay rise forecast 2027</td><td>5.0% (inflation %)</td><td>6th highest of 29</td></tr>\n<tr><td>State pension age</td><td>60 (Older Persons Grant)</td><td>5th lowest of 39</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Pension (share of pay)</td><td>8.9% of net pay</td><td>Lowest of 50</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Bank deposit protection</td><td>R100,000 per person, per bank</td><td>—</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Inheritance tax (children)</td><td>top rate 25%</td><td>—</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p><small>Rank compares South Africa with the other countries in each dataset; \"highest\" means the largest value. \"—\" means the measure isn't ranked.</small></p>\n\n<h2>Minimum Wage in South Africa (2026)</h2>\n<p>The legal minimum wage in South Africa is <strong>R30.23/hour</strong>. For a month of full-time work that is about <strong>$316</strong> at current exchange rates, 4th lowest of 38 countries in our comparison. From 1 March 2026.</p>\n<p>Full table for every country, with sources: <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/minimum-wage-by-country-2026-hourly-and.html\">Minimum Wage by Country 2026: Hourly and Monthly Rates in US Dollars</a>. <a href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/venkateshramu07-design/My_Repo@ccr-ee047f91-rbyv4x/seo/data/minimum-wage-2026.csv\">Download the data (CSV)</a>.</p>\n<h2>Pay Rises in South Africa: 2027 Forecast</h2>\n<p>Employers in South Africa expect to raise salaries by <strong>5.0%</strong> in 2027 (median of the major pay surveys), after 4.1% in 2026. With inflation at % (), that is roughly flat in real terms.</p>\n<p>Full table for every country, with sources: <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/salary-increase-forecasts-2027-by.html\">Salary Increase Forecasts 2027 by Country: Every Major Survey in One Table</a>. <a href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/venkateshramu07-design/My_Repo@ccr-ee047f91-rbyv4x/seo/data/salary-increase-forecasts-2027.csv\">Download the data (CSV)</a>.</p>\n<h2>Retirement Age in South Africa</h2>\n<p>The state pension age in South Africa is <strong>60 (Older Persons Grant)</strong> for people reaching it in 2026; the earliest you can claim is —. Future change: none legislated. Means-tested grant paid by SASSA.</p>\n<p>Full table for every country, with sources: <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/retirement-age-by-country-2026-state.html\">Retirement Age by Country 2026: State Pension Ages in 39 Countries</a>. <a href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/venkateshramu07-design/My_Repo@ccr-ee047f91-rbyv4x/seo/data/retirement-age-2026.csv\">Download the data (CSV)</a>.</p>\n<h2>How Much the State Pension Pays in South Africa</h2>\n<p>A full-career average earner in South Africa can expect a mandatory pension worth about <strong>8.9% of their previous net pay</strong>, the least generous of 50 countries we compare (OECD average 63.2%). Low earner (half the average wage): 17%. High earner (twice the average): 5%. Including common voluntary private pensions, an average earner would get 32%.</p>\n<p>Full table for every country, with sources: <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/state-pension-amounts-by-country-2026.html\">State Pension Amounts by Country 2026: How Much Retirees Actually Get</a>. <a href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/venkateshramu07-design/My_Repo@ccr-ee047f91-rbyv4x/seo/data/pension-net-replacement-rates.csv\">Download the data (CSV)</a>.</p>\n<h2>How Much of Your Money Is Protected in South Africa</h2>\n<p>Bank deposits in South Africa are protected up to <strong>R100,000</strong> per depositor, per bank (about $6,000), under the CODI scheme. Scheme launched April 2024. Money in payment apps and e-money wallets is usually not covered.</p>\n<p>Full table for every country, with sources: <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/deposit-insurance-limits-by-country.html\">Deposit Insurance Limits by Country 2026: How Much of Your Money Is Protected</a>. <a href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/venkateshramu07-design/My_Repo@ccr-ee047f91-rbyv4x/seo/data/deposit-insurance-limits-2026.csv\">Download the data (CSV)</a>.</p>\n<h2>Inheritance Tax in South Africa</h2>\n<p>South Africa has <strong>estate duty</strong>. Children can receive <strong>R3.5 million</strong> tax-free, and the top rate for children is <strong>25%</strong>, 10th highest of 28 countries. 20% above the abatement and 25% on estates above R30 million; spouses exempt.</p>\n<p>Full table for every country, with sources: <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/inheritance-tax-by-country-2026.html\">Inheritance Tax by Country 2026: Thresholds, Rates and Who Pays</a>. <a href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/venkateshramu07-design/My_Repo@ccr-ee047f91-rbyv4x/seo/data/inheritance-tax-2026.csv\">Download the data (CSV)</a>.</p>\n\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>\n<h3>What is the minimum wage in South Africa in 2026?</h3>\n<p>The minimum wage in South Africa is R30.23/hour, about $316 a month for full-time work. That is 4th lowest of 38 countries. From 1 March 2026.</p>\n<h3>What is the average pay rise in South Africa for 2027?</h3>\n<p>Pay surveys forecast an average salary increase of 5.0% in South Africa for 2027, against inflation of %.</p>\n<h3>What is the retirement age in South Africa?</h3>\n<p>The state pension age in South Africa is 60 (Older Persons Grant) in 2026, with the earliest claim at —. Legislated change: None legislated.</p>\n<h3>How much is the state pension in South Africa?</h3>\n<p>In South Africa, mandatory pensions replace about 8.9% of an average earner&#x27;s net pay after a full career, against an OECD average of 63.2%.</p>\n<h3>How much money is insured in a bank in South Africa?</h3>\n<p>Deposits in South Africa are insured up to R100,000 per person, per bank.</p>\n<h3>Is there inheritance tax in South Africa?</h3>\n<p>Yes. Children can inherit R3.5 million tax-free in South Africa; above that the top rate for children is 25%.</p>\n\n<h2>Compare South Africa With Other Countries</h2>\n<p>See every country side by side in <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/compare-countries-2026-minimum-wage-tax.html\">Compare Countries 2026: Minimum Wage, Tax, Mortgage Rates, Energy and Pension Age in 35 Countries</a>, or open a country page: <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/australia-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage.html\">Australia</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/austria-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage.html\">Austria</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/belgium-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage.html\">Belgium</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/brazil-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage.html\">Brazil</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/canada-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage-tax.html\">Canada</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/china-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage.html\">China</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/czechia-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage.html\">Czechia</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/denmark-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage.html\">Denmark</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/estonia-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage.html\">Estonia</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/finland-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage.html\">Finland</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/france-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage-tax.html\">France</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/germany-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage.html\">Germany</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/greece-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage-tax.html\">Greece</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/india-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage.html\">India</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/ireland-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage.html\">Ireland</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/italy-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage-tax.html\">Italy</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/japan-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage-tax.html\">Japan</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/latvia-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage-tax.html\">Latvia</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/lithuania-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage.html\">Lithuania</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/luxembourg-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage.html\">Luxembourg</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/mexico-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage-tax.html\">Mexico</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/the-netherlands-in-numbers-2026-minimum.html\">the Netherlands</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/new-zealand-in-numbers-2026-minimum.html\">New Zealand</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/norway-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage-tax.html\">Norway</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/poland-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage-tax.html\">Poland</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/portugal-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage.html\">Portugal</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/slovakia-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage.html\">Slovakia</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/slovenia-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage.html\">Slovenia</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/south-korea-in-numbers-2026-minimum.html\">South Korea</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/spain-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage-tax.html\">Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/sweden-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage-tax.html\">Sweden</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/switzerland-in-numbers-2026-tax.html\">Switzerland</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/the-united-kingdom-in-numbers-2026.html\">the United Kingdom</a>, <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/the-united-states-in-numbers-2026.html\">the United States</a>.</p>\n\n<div class=\"bd-cite\" style=\"margin:1.6em 0;padding:14px 16px;border-radius:14px;border:1px solid rgba(120,120,140,.25);font:500 14px/1.55 system-ui,sans-serif\"><b>Cite this page:</b> Blog Digest, &ldquo;South Africa Minimum Wage 2026 and Pension Age Compared&rdquo;, updated 25 October 2026, https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/south-africa-in-numbers-2026-minimum.html</div>\n<h2>Related Guides</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/minimum-wage-by-country-2026-hourly-and.html\">Minimum Wage by Country 2026: Hourly and Monthly Rates in US Dollars</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/salary-increase-forecasts-2027-by.html\">Salary Increase Forecasts 2027 by Country: Every Major Survey in One Table</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/retirement-age-by-country-2026-state.html\">Retirement Age by Country 2026: State Pension Ages in 39 Countries</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/state-pension-amounts-by-country-2026.html\">State Pension Amounts by Country 2026: How Much Retirees Actually Get</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/deposit-insurance-limits-by-country.html\">Deposit Insurance Limits by Country 2026: How Much of Your Money Is Protected</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/inheritance-tax-by-country-2026.html\">Inheritance Tax by Country 2026: Thresholds, Rates and Who Pays</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/how-much-emergency-fund-do-you-need.html\">How Much Emergency Fund Do You Need? (With Calculator)</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>Figures checked against the official sources listed in each linked guide in October 2026. Exchange-rate conversions are approximate. This page is for information and isn't financial or legal advice.</em></p>\n\n<script type=\"application/ld+json\" id=\"bd-faq-ld\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"FAQPage\", \"mainEntity\": [{\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What is the minimum wage in South Africa in 2026?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"The minimum wage in South Africa is R30.23/hour, about $316 a month for full-time work. That is 4th lowest of 38 countries. From 1 March 2026.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What is the average pay rise in South Africa for 2027?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Pay surveys forecast an average salary increase of 5.0% in South Africa for 2027, against inflation of %.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What is the retirement age in South Africa?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"The state pension age in South Africa is 60 (Older Persons Grant) in 2026, with the earliest claim at \\u2014. Legislated change: None legislated.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"How much is the state pension in South Africa?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"In South Africa, mandatory pensions replace about 8.9% of an average earner's net pay after a full career, against an OECD average of 63.2%.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"How much money is insured in a bank in South Africa?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Deposits in South Africa are insured up to R100,000 per person, per bank.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Is there inheritance tax in South Africa?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Yes. Children can inherit R3.5 million tax-free in South Africa; above that the top rate for children is 25%.\"}}]}</script>\n</div>",
